    "gaps": [
      "The selected main is expanded through shared native functions. Route preflight, dry-run, sticky aggregate and write audit remain outside this selected runner boundary; this graph does not return a route dispatch envelope.",
      "Child implementations remain native subprocess boundaries, including their finite draft/verification traversals and source-owned histories. Projected report schemas validate consumed interfaces and retain full native report content.",
      "Native subprocesses have no timeout. Lunar enforces the descriptor wall ceiling and 24-operation budget; these are not native subprocess timeouts.",
      "Lunar provides required runtime provenance and effect receipts. Native artifact writes and optional logging retain their source behavior. Compiler fixtures verify execution fidelity, not scientific validity or promotion readiness."
